1.8. **"Competing Use"** means making the Software or any Derivative Work available to others—whether free of charge or for a fee, and whether as source code, compiled binaries, an Android/iOS application, a software development kit (SDK), a library, an embedded firmware module, an API, or a managed/hosted service—that:
   (a) substitutes for the Software or any product or service offered by Licensor;
   (b) offers Competing Functionality, meaning a product or service that satisfies both of the following: (i) it is designed for, marketed for, or used for cellular network anomaly detection, IMSI-catcher or stingray detection, base-station trust scoring, or rogue/fake cell tower identification; AND (ii) it implements, incorporates, or is derived from five (5) or more of the method-families described in Section 1.4 (Detection Heuristics and Architecture) or the forty-two (42) detection methods documented in the Software, including but not limited to geographic anomaly detection, signal strength pattern analysis, timing advance anomaly detection, protocol downgrade detection, cipher suite validation, or trust scoring. For clarity, the five (5) method-family threshold is an evidentiary standard for establishing substantial similarity under this License, not a safe harbour permitting copying of fewer than five (5) methods; any unauthorized use, reproduction, or porting of even a single (1) detection method or heuristic constitutes a breach of this License. A party that has accessed, viewed, or downloaded the Software source code within the twenty-four (24) months preceding the alleged Competing Use shall be presumed to have copied such method-families, and any clean-room or independent-creation defence shall be unavailable to such party; or
