## 3. PERMITTED PURPOSE

A **"Permitted Purpose"** means only the following non-commercial activities performed by an individual natural person acting strictly in their private capacity:

3.1. **Personal Individual Security Use:** Personally compiling the Software from source Yourself and installing it onto a personal Android device owned and operated solely by You for Your own private, personal, non-commercial cellular security and privacy protection outside the scope of any employment, corporate, journalistic, or organizational mandate. You may not compile an APK once and install or sideload it onto devices belonging to other individuals, co-workers, or employees.

3.1A. **Incidental Benefit Safe Harbour:** A Permitted Purpose under Section 3.1 is not lost solely because Your personal, self-initiated use of the Software on Your own device incidentally benefits Your employer, journalistic work, or organizational activities, provided that all of the following conditions are satisfied: (a) Your use was not directed, required, encouraged, or mandated by any employer, organization, or supervisory policy; (b) no Mobile Device Management (MDM), Enterprise Mobility Management (EMM), or other automated or manual IT administration was used to install, push, or manage the Software on Your device; (c) You did not receive any reimbursement, stipend, or other compensation from any employer or organization for such use; and (d) no data, alerts, or output from the Software is reported, transmitted, or made available to any employer, organization, or third party. If any of conditions (a) through (d) is not satisfied, such use constitutes Internal Business or Organizational Use under Section 1.7 and requires a separate Commercial License Agreement.

3.2. **Non-Commercial Security Research & Academic Study:** Inspecting, auditing, testing, and analyzing the source code of the Software for non-commercial academic study, personal education, or independent vulnerability research, provided that any published research credits **Cymatune (https://github.com/lidarium/cymatune)** and does not distribute a Competing Use product.

3.3. **Non-Commercial Source Contributions & Authorized Coding Agents:** Creating modifications, refactoring, or bug fixes in a public fork on GitHub solely for personal testing or for submitting Pull Requests back to Licensor's official repository (including through the use of automated AI coding assistants or agents such as Jules, GitHub Copilot, or similar inference tools acting at the direction of Licensor or a Contributor to edit code or generate Pull Requests), provided that all original copyright, license, and attribution notices are retained intact.

